FIND: `bench/immune_agents.py`, `regulatory_t_cell_check()`. The autoimmune check’s model-bias detector counts only `REJECTED` findings, not `DUPLICATE` findings, even though the function’s own top-level safety metric defines removals as `rejected + duplicated`. Evidence: a model can have all its findings removed as duplicates, yielding total exclusion from the filtered set, but the bias check will not flag “all findings from one model rejected” because it ignores duplicates in `model_rejected`. This under-detects systematic suppression of one model by the NK/helper pipeline.

FIX: Count both `REJECTED` and `DUPLICATE` as removed findings in the per-model bias check and update the reason text accordingly.

